            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "Use cosine rule to show $x^{2}-6\\sqrt{3}\\,x+20=0$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$4^{2}=6^{2}+x^{2}-2(6)(x)\\cos30^{\\circ}$, so $x^{2}-6\\sqrt{3}\\,x+20=0$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4^{2}&=6^{2}+x^{2}-2(6)(x)\\cos30^{\\circ}\\\\16&=36+x^{2}-\\frac{12x\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\0&=20+x^{2}-6x\\sqrt{3}\\\\x^{2}-6\\sqrt{3}\\,x+20&=0\\end{align*}$$\nAs required.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 38
          },
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "Use the quadratic formula to show $AC$ has length $(3\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{7})\\,\\mathrm{cm}$ or $(3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{7})\\,\\mathrm{cm}$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$AC=(3\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{7})\\,\\mathrm{cm}$ or $(3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{7})\\,\\mathrm{cm}$, using the quadratic formula.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-6\\sqrt{3})\\pm\\sqrt{(-6\\sqrt{3})^{2}-4(1)(20)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{6\\sqrt{3}\\pm\\sqrt{28}}{2}\\\\x&=\\frac{6\\sqrt{3}\\pm2\\sqrt{7}}{2}\\\\x&=3\\sqrt{3}\\pm\\sqrt{7}\\end{align*}$$\nThus $AC=(3\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{7})\\,\\mathrm{cm}$ or $(3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{7})\\,\\mathrm{cm}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 55
          }
        ],
